# Atlantysm — contracts environment
#
# Copy to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in. Both the MUD CLI (`dotenv.config()`) and
# Foundry read this file, so one copy serves `mud deploy` and `forge script` alike.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED — the deployer
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Namespace owner of the World. `configureForge`, `setTokenFacades` and `setMintPrice` all require
# it, and PostDeploy reads it with vm.envUint("PRIVATE_KEY").
#
# Anvil's first account, safe to use locally and NOWHERE else:
PRIVATE_KEY=0xac0974bec39a17e36ba4a6b4d238ff944bacb478cbed5efcae784d7bf4f2ff80

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED FOR SEPOLIA — identity inputs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PostDeploy REVERTS on any chain other than anvil unless both of these are set. That guard is
# deliberate: `configureForge` freezes on the first mint, permanently, so a throwaway address here
# would bind every crystal ever minted to an implementation that does not exist — with no
# migration path, because nothing can ever call from the wrong address.
#
# The canonical ERC-6551 registry (v0.3.1). Verified deployed on Sepolia, and its selectors match
# src/accounts/IERC6551.sol exactly (createAccount 0x8a54c52f, account 0x246a0021).
# Use the canonical deployment, never your own copy: account addresses derive from it.
ERC6551_REGISTRY=0x000000006551c19487814612e58FE06813775758

# AtlantysmAccount, OUR implementation. Unlike the registry there is no canonical address — you
# deploy it yourself, once, and paste the address here BEFORE running the deploy.
# See step 3 of deploy_instructions.md.
ERC6551_ACCOUNT_IMPLEMENTATION=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mint price in wei. Defaults to 0.01 ether. Re-applied on every deploy, since it is an economic
# lever rather than an identity input, so it is the one setting you can change after the fact.
# MINT_PRICE=10000000000000000

# Etherscan key, only if you want `--verify` on the deploy.
# ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DO NOT SET `RPC_URL` HERE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MUD resolves the endpoint as:
#   FOUNDRY_ETH_RPC_URL || RPC_HTTP_URL || RPC_URL || <foundry profile>.eth_rpc_url || 127.0.0.1:8545
# so RPC_URL outranks every profile, including the absence of one. Left in this file it would make
# `pnpm deploy:local` deploy to Sepolia without a word of warning.
#
# Pass it inline, for the single command that needs it:
#   RPC_URL="https://eth-sepolia.g.alchemy.com/v2/<KEY>" pnpm deploy:sepolia
